      "math_academy_id": "q-214226",
      "sequence_position": 18,
      "problem": "Let $[\\,i\\,]_{195}$ denote the residue class modulo $195$ containing the element $i\\in Z.$ Select the correct options in the statements below.\n\n1. $\\,$ {{field-1}} $[\\,i\\,]_{195}=$ {{field-2}}\n\n2. $\\,$ $[\\,5\\,]_{195}$ {{field-3}} $[\\,127\\,]_{195}=$ {{field-4}}\n\n3. $\\,$ {{field-5}} $=\\{[\\,i\\,]_{195}\\,∣\\,${{field-6}} $\\le ${{field-7}} $<195\\}$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}=\\{[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following properties:\n\n1\\. ${⋃}_{i=0}^{194}\\,[\\,i\\,]_{195}=Z$\n\n2\\. $[\\,5\\,]_{195}\\cap [\\,127\\,]_{195}=∅$\n\n3\\. ${Z}_{195}=\\{[\\,i\\,]_{195}\\,∣\\,0\\le i<195\\}$",
